Fixed in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:686`:

```rust
let mut ret = (0usize, Some(0usize));

for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
    let hint = stream.size_hint();

    ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

    match (ret.1, hint.1) {
        (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
        (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
        _ => {}
    }
}
```

The accumulator previously used plain `+`, which panics on overflow in debug builds (and wraps in release, which is worse — a silently wrong hint). Now the lower bound saturates at `usize::MAX` and an overflowing upper bound degrades to `None`, i.e. "no known upper bound" — both still valid per the `size_hint` contract. The `0usize` annotation is needed because the literals were otherwise an ambiguous integer type and the methods wouldn't resolve.

`cargo test -p tokio-stream` passes in full, including the new `size_hint_overflow` test.
